#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:1
msgid "Advanced Attributes"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:3
msgid "Derivations can declare some infrequently used optional attributes."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:5
msgid "Inputs"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:7
msgid ""
"\\[`exportReferencesGraph`\\]{#adv-attr-exportReferencesGraph}  \n"
"Specifies the [_export references graph_](../store/derivation/index."
"md#export-references-graph) option. The value of this attribute should be a "
"list of pairs `[ name1 path1 name2 path2 ...  ]`. For example, when the "
"following derivation is built:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:12
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"derivation {\n"
"  ...\n"
"  exportReferencesGraph = [ \"libfoo-graph\" libfoo ];\n"
"};\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:19
msgid ""
"the references graph of `libfoo` is placed in the file `libfoo-graph` in the "
"temporary build directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:22
msgid ""
"\\[`passAsFile`\\]{#adv-attr-passAsFile}  \n"
"A list of names of attributes whose environment variables should be marked "
"[_pass as file_](../store/derivation/index.md#pass-as-file). For example, if "
"you have"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:27
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"passAsFile = [\"big\"];\n"
"big = \"a very long string\";\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:32
msgid ""
"then when the builder runs, the environment variable `bigPath` will contain "
"the absolute path to a temporary file containing `a very long string`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:36
msgid ""
"\\[`__structuredAttrs`\\]{#adv-attr-structuredAttrs}  \n"
"If the special attribute `__structuredAttrs` is set to `true`, the other "
"derivation attributes are serialised into a file in JSON format."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:40
msgid ""
"See the [corresponding section in the derivation page](../store/derivation/"
"index.md#structured-attrs) for further details."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:42
#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:250
#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:256
#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:288
msgid "**Warning**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:44
msgid ""
"If set to `true`, the top-level attributes [`allowedReferences`](#adv-attr-"
"allowedReferences), [`allowedRequisites`](#adv-attr-allowedRequisites), "
"[`disallowedReferences`](#adv-attr-disallowedReferences) and "
"[`disallowedRequisites`](#adv-attr-disallowedRequisites) will have no "
"effect; use [`outputChecks`](#adv-attr-outputChecks) instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:48
msgid "Output checks"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:50
msgid ""
"These attributes specify [checks on the derivation's outputs](../store/"
"derivation/outputs/index.md#output-checks). The concepts behind them are "
"documented there; this section gives the syntax for specifying them from the "
"Nix language."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:53
msgid ""
"Store paths in these lists may be given as strings with context (i.e. by "
"interpolating a derivation), and outputs of the derivation itself are "
"denoted by their plain output names, e.g. `\"out\"`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:55
msgid ""
"\\[`allowedReferences`\\]{#adv-attr-allowedReferences}  \n"
"Specifies the [_allowed references_](../store/derivation/outputs/index."
"md#allowed-references) check. For example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:62
msgid ""
"enforces that the output of a derivation cannot have any runtime "
"dependencies on its inputs. To allow an output to have a runtime dependency "
"on itself, use `\"out\"` as a list item."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:66
msgid ""
"\\[`allowedRequisites`\\]{#adv-attr-allowedRequisites}  \n"
"Specifies the [_allowed requisites_](../store/derivation/outputs/index."
"md#allowed-requisites) check. For example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:73
msgid ""
"enforces that the output of a derivation cannot have any other runtime "
"dependency than `foobar`, and in addition it enforces that `foobar` itself "
"doesn't introduce any other dependency itself."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:77
msgid ""
"\\[`disallowedReferences`\\]{#adv-attr-disallowedReferences}  \n"
"Specifies the [_disallowed references_](../store/derivation/outputs/index."
"md#disallowed-references) check. For example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:84
msgid ""
"enforces that the output of a derivation cannot have a direct runtime "
"dependency on the derivation `foo`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:87
msgid ""
"\\[`disallowedRequisites`\\]{#adv-attr-disallowedRequisites}  \n"
"Specifies the [_disallowed requisites_](../store/derivation/outputs/index."
"md#disallowed-requisites) check. For example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:94
msgid ""
"enforces that the output of a derivation cannot have any runtime dependency "
"on `foobar` or any other derivation depending recursively on `foobar`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:98
msgid ""
"\\[`outputChecks`\\]{#adv-attr-outputChecks}  \n"
"When using [structured attributes](#adv-attr-structuredAttrs), the "
"`outputChecks` attribute allows defining checks per-output."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:102
msgid ""
"In addition to [`allowedReferences`](#adv-attr-allowedReferences), "
"[`allowedRequisites`](#adv-attr-allowedRequisites), [`disallowedReferences`]"
"(#adv-attr-disallowedReferences) and [`disallowedRequisites`](#adv-attr-"
"disallowedRequisites), the following attributes are available:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:107
msgid ""
"`maxSize` specifies the [_max size_](../store/derivation/outputs/index."
"md#max-size) check."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:108
msgid ""
"`maxClosureSize` specifies the [_max closure size_](../store/derivation/"
"outputs/index.md#max-closure-size) check."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:109
msgid ""
"`ignoreSelfRefs` controls the [_ignore self references_](../store/derivation/"
"outputs/index.md#ignore-self-refs) behavior."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:111
#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:139
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:113
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"__structuredAttrs = true;\n"
"\n"
"outputChecks.out = {\n"
"  # The closure of 'out' must not be larger than 256 MiB.\n"
"  maxClosureSize = 256 * 1024 * 1024;\n"
"\n"
"  # It must not refer to the C compiler or to the 'dev' output.\n"
"  disallowedRequisites = [ stdenv.cc \"dev\" ];\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"outputChecks.dev = {\n"
"  # The 'dev' output must not be larger than 128 KiB.\n"
"  maxSize = 128 * 1024;\n"
"};\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:130
msgid "Other output modifications"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:132
msgid ""
"\\[`unsafeDiscardReferences`\\]{#adv-attr-unsafeDiscardReferences}  \n"
"When using [structured attributes](#adv-attr-structuredAttrs), the attribute "
"`unsafeDiscardReferences` is an attribute set with a boolean value for each "
"output name. If set to `true`, it enables the [_unsafe discard references_]"
"(../store/derivation/outputs/index.md#unsafe-discard-references) behavior "
"for that output."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:146
msgid "Build scheduling"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:148
msgid ""
"\\[`preferLocalBuild`\\]{#adv-attr-preferLocalBuild}  \n"
"If set to `true`, enables the [_prefer local build_](../store/derivation/"
"index.md#prefer-local-build) option. This is useful for derivations that are "
"cheapest to build locally."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:152
msgid ""
"\\[`allowSubstitutes`\\]{#adv-attr-allowSubstitutes}  \n"
"If set to `false`, disables the [_allow substitutes_](../store/derivation/"
"index.md#allow-substitutes) option, so Nix will always build this derivation "
"(locally or remotely) rather than substituting its outputs. This is useful "
"for derivations that are cheaper to build than to substitute."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:156
msgid ""
"\\[`requiredSystemFeatures`\\]{#adv-attr-requiredSystemFeatures}  \n"
"Specifies the [_required system features_](../store/derivation/index."
"md#required-system-features) option: Nix will only build the derivation on a "
"machine that has the corresponding features set in its [`system-features` "
"configuration](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-system-features)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:160
msgid "For example, setting"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:162
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"requiredSystemFeatures = [ \"kvm\" ];\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:166
msgid ""
"ensures that the derivation can only be built on a machine with the `kvm` "
"feature."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:168
msgid "Impure builder configuration"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:170
msgid ""
"\\[`impureEnvVars`\\]{#adv-attr-impureEnvVars}  \n"
"Specifies the [_impure environment variables_](../store/derivation/index."
"md#impure-env-vars) option: a list of environment variables that should be "
"passed from the environment of the calling user to the builder. For example, "
"`fetchurl` in Nixpkgs has the line"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:175
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"impureEnvVars = [ \"http_proxy\" \"https_proxy\" ... ];\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:179
msgid ""
"to make it use the proxy server configuration specified by the user in the "
"environment variables `http_proxy` and friends."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:182
msgid "Setting the derivation type"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:184
msgid ""
"As discussed in [Derivation Outputs and Types of Derivations](../store/"
"derivation/outputs/index.md), there are multiples kinds of derivations / "
"kinds of derivation outputs. The choice of the following attributes "
"determines which kind of derivation we are making."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:187
msgid "[`__contentAddressed`](#adv-attr-__contentAddressed)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:189
msgid "[`outputHash`](#adv-attr-outputHash)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:191
msgid "[`outputHashAlgo`](#adv-attr-outputHashAlgo)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:193
msgid "[`outputHashMode`](#adv-attr-outputHashMode)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:195
msgid ""
"The three types of derivations are chosen based on the following "
"combinations of these attributes. All other combinations are invalid."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:198
msgid ""
"[Input-addressing derivations](../store/derivation/outputs/input-address.md)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:200
msgid ""
"This is the default for `builtins.derivation`. Nix only currently supports "
"one kind of input-addressing, so no other information is needed."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:203
msgid ""
"`__contentAddressed = false;` may also be included, but is not needed, and "
"will trigger the experimental feature check."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:205
msgid ""
"[Fixed-output derivations](../glossary.md#gloss-fixed-output-derivation)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:207
msgid ""
"All of [`outputHash`](#adv-attr-outputHash), [`outputHashAlgo`](#adv-attr-"
"outputHashAlgo), and [`outputHashMode`](#adv-attr-outputHashMode)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:217
msgid ""
"[(Floating) content-addressing derivations](../store/derivation/outputs/"
"content-address.md)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:219
msgid ""
"Both [`outputHashAlgo`](#adv-attr-outputHashAlgo) and [`outputHashMode`]"
"(#adv-attr-outputHashMode), `__contentAddressed = true;`, and _not_ "
"`outputHash`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:221
msgid ""
"If an output hash was given, then the derivation output would be \"fixed\" "
"not \"floating\"."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:223
msgid ""
"Here is more information on the `output*` attributes, and what values they "
"may be set to:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:225
msgid "[`outputHashMode`](#adv-attr-outputHashMode){#adv-attr-outputHashMode}"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:227
msgid ""
"This specifies how the files of a content-addressing derivation output are "
"digested to produce a content address."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:229
msgid ""
"This works in conjunction with [`outputHashAlgo`](#adv-attr-outputHashAlgo). "
"Specifying one without the other is an error (unless \\[`outputHash` is also "
"specified and includes its own hash algorithm as described below)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:232
msgid ""
"The `outputHashMode` attribute determines how the hash is computed. It must "
"be one of the following values:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:235
msgid "[`\"flat\"`](../store/store-object/content-address.md#method-flat)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:237
msgid "This is the default."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:239
msgid ""
"[`\"recursive\"` or `\"nar\"`](../store/store-object/content-address."
"md#method-nix-archive)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:241
msgid "**Compatibility**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:243
msgid ""
"`\"recursive\"` is the traditional way of indicating this, and is supported "
"since 2005 (virtually the entire history of Nix). `\"nar\"` is more clear, "
"and consistent with other parts of Nix (such as the CLI), however support "
"for it is only added in Nix version 2.21."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:248
msgid "[`\"text\"`](../store/store-object/content-address.md#method-text)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:252
msgid ""
"The use of this method for derivation outputs is part of the [`dynamic-"
"derivations`](../development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-dynamic-"
"derivations) experimental feature."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:254
msgid "[`\"git\"`](../store/store-object/content-address.md#method-git)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:258
msgid ""
"This method is part of the [`git-hashing`](../development/experimental-"
"features.md#xp-feature-git-hashing) experimental feature."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:260
msgid ""
"See [content-addressing store objects](../store/store-object/content-address."
"md) for more information about the process this flag controls."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:262
msgid "[`outputHashAlgo`](#adv-attr-outputHashAlgo){#adv-attr-outputHashAlgo}"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:264
msgid ""
"This specifies the hash algorithm used to digest the [file system object](../"
"store/file-system-object.md) data of a content-addressing derivation output."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:266
msgid ""
"This works in conjunction with [`outputHashMode`](#adv-attr-outputHashAlgo). "
"Specifying one without the other is an error (unless `outputHash` is also "
"specified and includes its own hash algorithm as described below)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:269
msgid ""
"The `outputHashAlgo` attribute specifies the hash algorithm used to compute "
"the hash. It can currently be `\"blake3\"`, `\"sha1\"`, `\"sha256\"`, "
"`\"sha512\"`, or `null`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:272
msgid ""
"`outputHashAlgo` can only be `null` when `outputHash` follows the SRI "
"format, because in that case the choice of hash algorithm is determined by "
"`outputHash`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:274
msgid "[`outputHash`](#adv-attr-outputHash){#adv-attr-outputHash}"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:276
msgid ""
"This will specify the output hash of the single output of a [fixed-output "
"derivation](../glossary.md#gloss-fixed-output-derivation)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:278
msgid ""
"The `outputHash` attribute must be a string containing the hash in either "
"hexadecimal or \"nix32\" encoding, or following the format for integrity "
"metadata as defined by [SRI](../glossary.md#gloss-sri). The [\"nix32\" "
"encoding](../protocols/nix32.md) is Nix's variant of Base32 encoding."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:281
msgid "**Note**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:283
msgid ""
"The [`convertHash`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-convertHash) function "
"shows how to convert between different encodings. The [`nix-hash` command]"
"(../command-ref/nix-hash.md) has information about obtaining the hash for "
"some contents, as well as converting to and from encodings."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:286
msgid ""
"[`__contentAddressed`](#adv-attr-__contentAddressed){#adv-attr-"
"\\_\\_contentAddressed}"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:290
msgid ""
"This attribute is part of an [experimental feature](../development/"
"experimental-features.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:292
msgid ""
"To use this attribute, you must enable the \\[`ca-derivations`\\]\\[xp-"
"feature-ca-derivations\\] experimental feature. For example, in [nix.conf]"
"(../command-ref/conf-file.md) you could add:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/advanced-attributes.md:300
msgid ""
"This is a boolean with a default of `false`. It determines whether the "
"derivation is floating content-addressing."
msgstr ""
